   (non-exhaustive) the longitudinal planner and controllers, the Toyota car port (carcontroller, carstate) and the
   user interface. The git history records every change, its author and its date.

3. Main features developed by cgw1968acc for the Toyota Corolla Altis Hybrid, including: smooth stopping and
   end-of-stop force control, creep and stall handling, lead braking assistance and sticky radar lead, stop gap
   closing and holding, night gap, cruise smoothing, low-speed lane centering and straight hold, lateral torque
   split, door unlock when shifting into P, and the tn_autoupdate updater.

